      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "Cpanel::JSON::XS versions before 4.80 for Perl allow memory exhaustion by buffering incremental input past max_size in incr_parse.\n\nThe parser appends each chunk to its buffer. In scalar or list context, it compares max_size with how far it has progressed, not with the buffer length. A chunk that starts with a NUL byte stops the parser before it progresses, and a call in void context skips the check, so the buffer grows without limit.\n\nA peer streaming data to an incr_parse consumer can exhaust process memory regardless of max_size.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
